            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral renal dysplasia, hydronephrosis, and hydroureter in a septic neonatal foal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>257-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A Canadian warmblood foal treated for septic polyarthritis was diagnosed with bilateral congenital renal dysplasia, hydronephrosis, and hydroureter at 2 weeks of age based on abdominal ultrasound and postmortem examination. Intermittent abdominal pain throughout the course of treatment was attributed to hydronephrosis and hydroureter.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
